1
00:00:16,892 --> 00:00:18,393
<i>Jump.</i>

2
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:49,216
Hmm.

3
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:45,897
Hello.

4
00:01:50,694 --> 00:01:52,362
I'm here for the interview.

5
00:01:53,739 --> 00:01:56,074
- Please have a seat inside.
- Yeah

6
00:02:01,163 --> 00:02:02,164
I'll be back

7
00:02:38,033 --> 00:02:39,284
You haven't moved.

8
00:02:40,327 --> 00:02:41,662
I was told to wait.

9
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:48,293
Did you stay here all night?

10
00:02:49,002 --> 00:02:50,295
You said, "Have a seat."

11
00:03:00,222 --> 00:03:01,682
Do you know who I am?

12
00:03:03,225 --> 00:03:04,685
I have a pretty good idea.

13
00:03:05,352 --> 00:03:06,269
You're a Guardian.

14
00:03:06,353 --> 00:03:07,938
And what have you been
told about us?

15
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:10,982
You are the ruling body
of the cosmos,

16
00:03:11,650 --> 00:03:12,859
founder of the Lanterns.

17
00:03:12,943 --> 00:03:14,111
There were 12 of you.

18
00:03:14,152 --> 00:03:15,654
One of you recently died.

19
00:03:16,238 --> 00:03:17,447
My condolences.

20
00:03:17,489 --> 00:03:18,532
Thank you.

21
00:03:19,783 --> 00:03:22,160
Also, you're all blue.

22
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:27,165
We believe this interview
will be more pleasurable...

23
00:03:28,834 --> 00:03:30,627
if I am in human form.

24
00:03:30,669 --> 00:03:32,629
- May I ask you a question?
- Please.

25
00:03:32,671 --> 00:03:36,216
Green Lanterns
are chosen by rings.

26
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:39,177
So why, suddenly, are you
interviewing people for the job?

27
00:03:39,261 --> 00:03:41,054
Because of your condolences.

28
00:03:47,185 --> 00:03:49,187
Am I supposed to say something?

29
00:03:49,271 --> 00:03:52,190
This is when most candidates
ask, "Why me?"

30
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:53,984
Oh.

31
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:56,695
No. I know exactly why me.

32
00:04:01,742 --> 00:04:03,034
Mama!

33
00:04:06,872 --> 00:04:08,039
Mama!

34
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:10,876
I'm coming, Marcus.

35
00:04:26,475 --> 00:04:28,560
<i>Are you afraid?</i>

36
00:04:28,643 --> 00:04:30,061
Yes!

37
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:32,189
Yes!

38
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:41,531
What happened?

39
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:46,036
Oh my God.

40
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:04,888
<i>The mysterious hero
known only as Green Lantern</i>

41
00:05:04,930 --> 00:05:08,058
<i>has again saved a major city
from near catastrophe.</i>

42
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:10,227
<i>Still no information exists
about his identity,</i>

43
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:12,395
<i>but today, he has offered
this statement.</i>

44
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:15,607
<i>Quoting now,
"Though you can't see my face,</i>

45
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:17,609
<i>know that my commitment
to fighting evil</i>

46
00:05:17,692 --> 00:05:19,027
<i>will never waver.</i>

47
00:05:19,069 --> 00:05:22,280
<i>The night I received this ring,
I was asked only one question,</i>

48
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:24,074
<i>if I was afraid.</i>

49
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:26,952
<i>I remain as steadfast now
as I was then.</i>

50
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:28,912
<i>I am fearless."</i>

51
00:05:33,208 --> 00:05:35,919
Are you out of your mind?

52
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:38,129
How the fuck was I not supposed
to be scared?

53
00:05:38,213 --> 00:05:39,923
Got lifted out of my bed.

54
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:42,801
- I was in a... a bubble.
- Give me the gun, Johnny.

55
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:44,052
The light was green.

56
00:05:44,970 --> 00:05:46,763
It was a test

57
00:05:46,805 --> 00:05:49,474
to be this Lantern thing,
and they wanted me.

58
00:05:49,558 --> 00:05:51,434
We have been through this.
It was a nightmare.

59
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:53,812
- There was no bubble!
- There was. He just said it.

60
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:55,605
Give me the pistol, Johnny.

61
00:05:55,689 --> 00:05:57,566
They asked him the same thing
they asked me.

62
00:05:57,649 --> 00:05:58,942
Oh, you think
that's a coincidence?

63
00:05:59,025 --> 00:06:01,152
- You're scaring me.
- "Are you afraid?"

64
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,115
Why you don't believe me?

65
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:07,284
Because it's unbelievable!

66
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:09,160
But you better believe
if you don't hand me that gun,

67
00:06:09,244 --> 00:06:10,912
I will send you to your maker!

68
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:23,383
I... I wasn't
gonna hurt nobody, Bernie.

69
00:06:26,845 --> 00:06:29,014
This thing
has got your mind gone,

70
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:30,724
and we can't do this anymore.

71
00:06:30,807 --> 00:06:32,100
And when we come home
from school,

72
00:06:32,183 --> 00:06:33,393
you better be gone!

73
00:06:54,873 --> 00:06:57,375
Is Sergeant Stewart available?

74
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:00,211
He's not.

75
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:02,213
Can I help you?

76
00:07:02,297 --> 00:07:05,258
- At what hour do you expect him?
- I'm not sure.

77
00:07:07,218 --> 00:07:08,511
Who are you?

78
00:07:08,553 --> 00:07:10,472
Are you Sergeant Stewart's wife?

79
00:07:11,389 --> 00:07:13,558
- Bernadette.
- Please tell your husband

80
00:07:13,642 --> 00:07:16,144
the Guardians
send their deepest regrets

81
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:18,355
for any lingering trauma

82
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:21,983
caused by
our latest communication.

83
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:24,569
We would like
to make compensation

84
00:07:24,653 --> 00:07:28,323
for any continued distress
that may have resulted.

85
00:07:31,618 --> 00:07:34,079
I don't understand,
I...

86
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:39,376
We have reports
that many of the candidates

87
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:41,670
considered for the role
of Green Lantern

88
00:07:41,753 --> 00:07:43,254
have been experiencing...

89
00:07:45,757 --> 00:07:47,175
emotional turmoil.

90
00:07:49,427 --> 00:07:51,554
Are you telling me
you're an alien?

91
00:07:51,638 --> 00:07:55,475
I am an intergalactic species
non-native to your Earth, yes.

92
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:56,643
Prove it.

93
00:07:57,811 --> 00:07:59,062
Excuse me?

94
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:02,774
You just look like some
unfortunate White lady to me.

95
00:08:03,566 --> 00:08:04,651
Prove it.

96
00:08:08,279 --> 00:08:10,448
I've found my natural form

97
00:08:11,157 --> 00:08:13,034
to be upsetting to humans.

98
00:08:14,786 --> 00:08:15,954
I don't get upset.

99
00:08:17,122 --> 00:08:18,289
Show me.

100
00:08:51,031 --> 00:08:52,490
You drink coffee?

101
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:58,705
Sorry for the mess.
My kids just had a test.

102
00:08:59,998 --> 00:09:02,208
You have more children
than this?

103
00:09:02,292 --> 00:09:05,420
I do. I meant my students.
I'm a teacher.

104
00:09:06,629 --> 00:09:09,841
So, you floated my husband
out of our bed?

105
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:12,343
We have never had
a Green Lantern from Earth.

106
00:09:14,345 --> 00:09:17,307
We realize now that
the ring's selection process

107
00:09:17,348 --> 00:09:18,725
is unusual

108
00:09:19,851 --> 00:09:21,269
for your species.

109
00:09:21,352 --> 00:09:23,229
Do you all intend
on fixing this?

110
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:27,901
Everyone he talks to thinks
Johnny's lost his mind.

111
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:30,111
He's nearly drinking himself
to death every night.

112
00:09:30,153 --> 00:09:32,030
My family is falling apart.

113
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:35,867
The system is imperfect.
This is the best I can do.

114
00:09:37,702 --> 00:09:40,121
Do you know the differences
in race on Earth?

115
00:09:41,081 --> 00:09:44,000
Do you understand
how unfair it is

116
00:09:44,084 --> 00:09:46,836
to ask a Black man in America
if he's afraid?

117
00:09:48,546 --> 00:09:49,881
By "Black," you mean...

118
00:09:51,549 --> 00:09:53,093
brown skin?

119
00:09:53,176 --> 00:09:55,678
We are terrified daily
of persecution

120
00:09:55,762 --> 00:09:58,306
and still show up,
sometimes better,

121
00:09:58,348 --> 00:10:00,683
than everyone around us.
Did you know that?

122
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:04,229
I did not.

123
00:10:05,647 --> 00:10:07,607
Even in space,
y'all don't consider us.

124
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:17,742
Humans have
relatively short lifespans.

125
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:24,207
Perhaps this could
present opportunities.

126
00:10:25,250 --> 00:10:26,709
Whatever the ring saw
in your husband

127
00:10:26,793 --> 00:10:31,005
is in his genetic makeup.
You are a very formidable woman.

128
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:35,343
Your offspring could one day...

129
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,471
be an excellent candidate.

130
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:45,019
That's a long time from now.
What... what if he's scared too?

131
00:10:45,103 --> 00:10:46,271
Then he'd fail.

132
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:51,442
And if I raise him
to be fearless?

133
00:10:52,944 --> 00:10:55,196
That would certainly warrant
our attention...

134
00:10:57,365 --> 00:10:58,491
when the time came.

135
00:10:59,701 --> 00:11:01,286
And when the time comes,

136
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:05,165
how do I know
he'll get a fair shot?

137
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:07,375
You have my word.

138
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:22,473
Were you the one
that came to visit my mom?

139
00:11:22,557 --> 00:11:23,600
Yes.

140
00:11:23,641 --> 00:11:25,935
You know,
the police came to visit her

141
00:11:25,977 --> 00:11:28,229
when she tried
to cash that diamond.

142
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:30,440
They didn't believe it was hers.

143
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:33,026
I am sorry
she had to go through that.

144
00:11:34,611 --> 00:11:36,362
Yeah, I'll pass that along.

145
00:11:36,446 --> 00:11:38,948
Your father was a Marine.
Is that why you became one too?

146
00:11:39,032 --> 00:11:42,452
Yes, ma'am.
And it's, uh, part of the path.

147
00:11:42,493 --> 00:11:43,453
The path?

148
00:11:43,536 --> 00:11:46,289
I became a Marine
so I could get here,

149
00:11:46,331 --> 00:11:47,665
across the table from you.

150
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:51,336
Well, let's start there,
John Stewart.

151
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:55,882
Or, Sergeant Major John Stewart.

152
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:59,219
- Is that right?
- Formerly Sergeant Major.

153
00:12:13,691 --> 00:12:15,735
You don't have other clothes
in your car, uh...?

154
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:17,737
- Gym bag?
- No, sir.

155
00:12:19,072 --> 00:12:22,492
Well, I ordered.
I got you a steak and a beer.

156
00:12:22,533 --> 00:12:25,954
- Thank you.
- Weren't supposed to be dressed.

157
00:12:26,037 --> 00:12:28,456
I was told this was about
an issue of national security.

158
00:12:28,539 --> 00:12:31,084
The whole point of meeting
at an Outback is to be discreet.

159
00:12:35,088 --> 00:12:37,048
Not a lot of snipers
like you left.

160
00:12:37,131 --> 00:12:38,549
Your kill record's impeccable.

161
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:40,969
- You're patient.
- Is this my target?

162
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,389
Code name is Gray Wolf.

163
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:46,099
- He launders money.
- I don't care about the man.

164
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:49,477
- Tell me about the mission.
- He's impossible to track.

165
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:51,854
There's only one place
we've ever known him to return.

166
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:54,691
A retreat we believe he owns
in the Kamchatka Peninsula.

167
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:57,694
We have no idea how often
he goes, how long he stays.

168
00:12:57,735 --> 00:13:01,781
You want me to wait on him,
stay there until he shows up.

169
00:13:01,864 --> 00:13:04,492
It could take weeks,
maybe a couple months.

170
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:05,910
And how many have been
before me?

171
00:13:07,578 --> 00:13:09,038
What makes you think
you're not the first?

172
00:13:09,122 --> 00:13:10,248
Well, there's intel

173
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:11,874
on an otherwise remote
mountain range,

174
00:13:11,958 --> 00:13:13,376
a rudimentary map
of the retreat,

175
00:13:13,418 --> 00:13:14,460
so someone's been there.

176
00:13:15,795 --> 00:13:17,463
Three.

177
00:13:17,547 --> 00:13:20,508
We lost contact
with the last team months ago.

178
00:13:20,550 --> 00:13:22,760
But if you agree to the mission,
we'll do things differently.

179
00:13:22,844 --> 00:13:24,721
You'll have a panic button
if you need extraction.

180
00:13:24,804 --> 00:13:28,099
I don't want that.
I don't do panic, sir.

181
00:13:31,394 --> 00:13:33,104
Best to get your affairs
in order before you leave.

182
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:34,939
- Yeah.
- How's your dad?

183
00:13:36,107 --> 00:13:37,567
Sir?

184
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:40,278
We were stationed together
after... after basic, uh...

185
00:13:41,070 --> 00:13:42,238
I heard he had some struggles.

186
00:13:45,825 --> 00:13:48,202
Much better, sir. Thank you.

187
00:14:05,762 --> 00:14:07,305
I didn't hear you come in.

188
00:14:08,014 --> 00:14:10,058
Couch getting too comfortable?

189
00:14:10,141 --> 00:14:12,018
It's better than a motel.

190
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:16,731
We need to fix this, Johnny.

191
00:14:17,732 --> 00:14:19,192
I know.

192
00:14:19,275 --> 00:14:21,152
You were never
gonna wear that ring.

193
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:23,613
- I know you don't believe me.
- I do now.

194
00:14:23,654 --> 00:14:25,865
And I'm sorry that
everybody's been treating you

195
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:27,033
like you're crazy.

196
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:32,330
- I'm sorry I have.
- Why now? What changed?

197
00:14:47,512 --> 00:14:50,431
One of the Green Lantern's
bosses came by the other day.

198
00:14:51,599 --> 00:14:53,851
They apologized
for not picking you.

199
00:15:02,693 --> 00:15:04,821
What did they say?

200
00:15:04,862 --> 00:15:07,615
Some bullshit about
the imperfection of the system.

201
00:15:10,701 --> 00:15:12,120
But it could be John.

202
00:15:14,122 --> 00:15:15,164
Our baby?

203
00:15:16,499 --> 00:15:19,127
- That's right.
- Huh.

204
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:22,255
- I don't understand.
- Why did you become a Marine?

205
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:26,217
Why do I get up and teach?

206
00:15:27,677 --> 00:15:30,012
To be better
than where we came from,

207
00:15:30,096 --> 00:15:32,723
to prove to God-knows-who
that we are worth a damn.

208
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:35,726
And we didn't break
every stereotype

209
00:15:35,810 --> 00:15:38,688
and face down every fear
for you to be penalized

210
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:41,190
because you're scared to leave
the people that you love.

211
00:15:41,274 --> 00:15:43,484
They don't see us, Bernie,
and you know that.

212
00:15:44,902 --> 00:15:46,195
Down here or up there.

213
00:15:46,279 --> 00:15:47,864
I said the same thing,

214
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,449
but we can't accept that.

215
00:15:50,408 --> 00:15:51,909
We can't raise three boys

216
00:15:51,993 --> 00:15:53,744
and believe that no matter
how good they are,

217
00:15:53,828 --> 00:15:56,998
- they get looked over.
- Why not Aaron or Marcus?

218
00:15:57,081 --> 00:15:59,375
No, they're too old. Um...

219
00:15:59,417 --> 00:16:00,793
They already know fear.

220
00:16:03,796 --> 00:16:06,048
Plus, I think
the Guardian liked John.

221
00:16:07,383 --> 00:16:08,926
I could tell.

222
00:16:14,265 --> 00:16:16,225
How do you make a Green Lantern?

223
00:16:18,019 --> 00:16:19,061
I've been reading.

224
00:16:20,855 --> 00:16:22,940
We condition him
so he's used to fear.

225
00:16:23,983 --> 00:16:26,068
Train him to be everything
they saw in you

226
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:28,321
and everything
the Lantern they picked isn't.

227
00:16:31,407 --> 00:16:32,492
I don't know.

228
00:16:36,037 --> 00:16:37,747
The night that they rejected you

229
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:40,625
was the beginning
of everything falling apart.

230
00:16:43,169 --> 00:16:45,630
This is a chance for us
to put it back together.

231
00:16:54,805 --> 00:16:56,098
He's gonna hate us.

232
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:58,434
So be it.

233
00:17:16,369 --> 00:17:18,996
It's not ideal jumping weather,
but it's the only way they don't see us.

234
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:20,456
Then it's ideal.

235
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:22,375
When the mission is complete,
hit this button.

236
00:17:22,458 --> 00:17:24,585
If anything goes wrong
and you need extraction...

237
00:17:24,627 --> 00:17:26,420
You'll hear from me
when the mission's complete.

238
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:28,673
Good luck. Jump.

239
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:43,914
I was dishonorably discharged.

240
00:18:44,999 --> 00:18:46,751
- Elaborate.
- Which part?

241
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:48,669
The dishonorable
or the discharge?

242
00:18:48,753 --> 00:18:50,379
I am more concerned
with disobedience.

243
00:18:50,463 --> 00:18:52,089
No disobedience.

244
00:18:52,173 --> 00:18:54,342
I had a mission to complete
and I failed.

245
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:59,221
You don't present as someone
who relents without cause.

246
00:18:59,263 --> 00:19:02,600
Well, if there was a reason
or a cause,

247
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:04,226
that would be classified.

248
00:19:07,063 --> 00:19:10,399
Much of what I will discuss
will also be classified.

249
00:19:10,441 --> 00:19:12,360
You have my word
nothing leaves this room.

250
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:19,075
What do you know about Sinestro?

251
00:19:19,158 --> 00:19:22,411
Only what I saw on the news.
He went rogue.

252
00:19:22,453 --> 00:19:25,081
He killed
one of your fellow Guardians.

253
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:27,166
Hal Jordan beat his ass
and locked him up.

254
00:19:27,249 --> 00:19:28,584
And what do you think
of Hal Jordan?

255
00:19:28,668 --> 00:19:30,211
- I don't.
- You don't what?

256
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:33,005
- I don't think about him.
- You must think something.

257
00:19:34,131 --> 00:19:35,925
He was chosen
instead of your father.

258
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:39,261
My dad served
this country honorably.

259
00:19:39,345 --> 00:19:40,888
He respects anyone
whose job it is

260
00:19:40,930 --> 00:19:43,683
to protect people.
He taught me to do the same.

261
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:49,438
Sinestro was Jordan's teacher.

262
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:51,482
A father figure.

263
00:19:53,651 --> 00:19:56,112
He still harbors deep affection
for his mentor.

264
00:19:56,153 --> 00:19:57,154
It's quite...

265
00:20:00,449 --> 00:20:01,617
troubling.

266
00:20:01,659 --> 00:20:03,244
It's human.

267
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:05,621
We love the people
that raise us.

268
00:20:08,416 --> 00:20:10,793
Even if they're crazy.

269
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:32,940
Make a wish, my boy.

270
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:38,612
We got something for you, baby.
Close your eyes.

271
00:20:38,696 --> 00:20:40,656
Why are you closing
your eyes, Marcus?

272
00:20:40,698 --> 00:20:42,491
I want it be a baseball jersey.

273
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:44,243
You can't fit your gut
in John's shirts.

274
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:46,203
Hey.

275
00:20:46,287 --> 00:20:48,080
- Open it.
- Whoa!

276
00:20:59,049 --> 00:21:02,011
Wait, I asked for crayons.

277
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:04,346
Your father and I think
five is old enough

278
00:21:04,388 --> 00:21:05,556
to know about your destiny.

279
00:21:17,735 --> 00:21:20,070
You're gonna be the Green Lantern
when you grow up, son.

280
00:21:22,573 --> 00:21:25,493
You probably wondered
why we treat you so different.

281
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:27,703
Sleep in a different room
than your brothers,

282
00:21:27,745 --> 00:21:29,205
don't go to school with them.

283
00:21:29,246 --> 00:21:30,539
I thought
you just liked him better.

284
00:21:30,623 --> 00:21:31,707
Hey!

285
00:21:31,791 --> 00:21:33,250
Boys, this is serious.

286
00:21:35,252 --> 00:21:37,838
When you were a baby,
the Guardians,

287
00:21:37,922 --> 00:21:40,049
the people
that run the whole universe,

288
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:42,176
came to tell us
that they want you

289
00:21:42,259 --> 00:21:44,053
to be the next Green Lantern.

290
00:21:44,094 --> 00:21:45,721
They said that
we had to train you

291
00:21:45,805 --> 00:21:48,224
and they would send birds
to watch over us.

292
00:21:48,265 --> 00:21:49,892
They report back
to the Guardians.

293
00:21:49,975 --> 00:21:53,229
That's why
you like birds so much, son.

294
00:21:53,312 --> 00:21:55,898
Now, I know you like drawing,
and you wanted those crayons,

295
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:57,650
and you can still do that
a little.

296
00:21:58,567 --> 00:22:01,445
But this year,
your real training starts.

297
00:22:01,529 --> 00:22:02,863
What do I have to do?

298
00:22:04,615 --> 00:22:06,784
They want us to make sure
that you're fearless.

299
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:09,578
- You always choose him.
- Hey, Aaron.

300
00:22:12,289 --> 00:22:13,290
Hey.

301
00:22:15,334 --> 00:22:17,586
You can't worry about him.

302
00:22:17,628 --> 00:22:19,964
You can't worry about anybody
but yourself.

303
00:22:20,881 --> 00:22:22,424
You don't want
the Guardians to think

304
00:22:22,466 --> 00:22:25,386
- you don't wanna do it, right?
- No, ma'am.

305
00:22:28,514 --> 00:22:29,598
What's this?

306
00:22:29,682 --> 00:22:31,976
Careful, Marcus.
Hand it to John.

307
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:37,606
We've given you
your target, son.

308
00:22:38,482 --> 00:22:41,026
Now you gotta learn to shoot.
You ready?

309
00:22:42,194 --> 00:22:44,697
Is that why you chose
to be a sniper?

310
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:47,575
- Uh, I'm a good shot.
- That is not what I'm asking.

311
00:22:48,993 --> 00:22:52,621
I can hit a target
from over a mile away.

312
00:23:06,635 --> 00:23:08,345
<i>So, you like the distance?</i>

313
00:23:10,681 --> 00:23:11,932
<i>Is that a metaphor?</i>

314
00:23:12,850 --> 00:23:15,978
<i>You asking me
if I'm close to anyone,</i>

315
00:23:16,061 --> 00:23:18,063
<i>or if I'll be distracted
on the job?</i>

316
00:23:19,189 --> 00:23:20,733
<i>Yes.</i>

317
00:23:20,816 --> 00:23:21,942
<i>That is what I'm asking.</i>

318
00:23:25,195 --> 00:23:28,449
<i>I like being alone,
and I don't get distracted.</i>

319
00:23:35,956 --> 00:23:37,041
<i>And your parents?</i>

320
00:23:40,210 --> 00:23:42,129
Do you resent them
for the rigors of your training?

321
00:23:43,088 --> 00:23:44,340
Do you have a family?

322
00:23:44,423 --> 00:23:48,510
We come into existence alone,
and we die the same.

323
00:23:49,678 --> 00:23:50,721
That's sad.

324
00:23:52,890 --> 00:23:54,850
Is it?

325
00:23:54,934 --> 00:23:59,855
I can't really explain family
to someone who doesn't have one,

326
00:23:59,897 --> 00:24:03,567
but rigorous kind of comes
with the territory.

327
00:24:05,319 --> 00:24:08,489
Hey, that was good, boy.
That was real good.

328
00:24:08,572 --> 00:24:10,699
Go on over there
and set up another apple.

329
00:24:10,783 --> 00:24:12,368
Aren't you supposed
to be out here

330
00:24:12,409 --> 00:24:13,702
finishing this dish?

331
00:24:13,744 --> 00:24:15,496
I thought
it made more sense to train.

332
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:17,039
You thought?

333
00:24:17,081 --> 00:24:19,249
There's nothing to think about.
We have to finish the dish.

334
00:24:19,333 --> 00:24:22,252
Diamond money's gone, Bernie.
We still need more parts.

335
00:24:22,336 --> 00:24:23,379
And I need to call 'em

336
00:24:23,462 --> 00:24:24,546
and tell 'em
how good he's doing.

337
00:24:24,588 --> 00:24:25,798
We don't even know who to call,

338
00:24:25,881 --> 00:24:27,549
and they said
they'll be watching.

339
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:29,051
I'm not leaving this up to them.

340
00:24:29,134 --> 00:24:31,345
Look, Daddy. Like William Tell.

341
00:24:32,554 --> 00:24:34,431
Shoot one off me.

342
00:24:39,019 --> 00:24:40,688
Do it.

343
00:24:40,771 --> 00:24:43,273
- What?
- See if he's afraid. Do it.

344
00:24:56,370 --> 00:24:57,621
Fear is contagious.

345
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:01,000
Ask him what they asked you.

346
00:25:13,012 --> 00:25:14,763
Are you afraid?

347
00:25:14,847 --> 00:25:15,973
No, sir.

348
00:25:22,312 --> 00:25:23,647
This is what it takes.

349
00:25:24,606 --> 00:25:25,858
For the both of you.

350
00:25:36,035 --> 00:25:38,871
It's applesauce. Can I eat some?

351
00:25:40,497 --> 00:25:42,499
I think your father
can do better than that.

352
00:25:44,334 --> 00:25:46,128
You deserve
a cheeseburger, boy.

353
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:48,797
My boy. Come on.

354
00:25:52,509 --> 00:25:55,929
<i>And your parents,
do you love them?</i>

355
00:25:55,971 --> 00:26:00,017
Yes. Of course, I love them.
I owe them everything.

356
00:26:00,100 --> 00:26:02,436
- You owe them?
- Yes.

357
00:26:02,478 --> 00:26:05,189
And how do you intend
to repay them?

358
00:26:05,272 --> 00:26:07,775
- By getting this job.
- And what if you don't?

359
00:26:08,442 --> 00:26:09,985
I will.

360
00:26:10,069 --> 00:26:13,655
- How can you be so sure?
- I was trained to be sure.

361
00:26:50,484 --> 00:26:52,277
You trippin'.

362
00:26:52,361 --> 00:26:54,530
- No, I know I'm right.
- That's not what it says.

363
00:26:54,571 --> 00:26:55,614
- Says.
- Yes, it is.

364
00:26:55,697 --> 00:26:57,574
They just can't say the "S" word
on the radio.

365
00:26:57,658 --> 00:26:59,034
Are the real words to this song,

366
00:26:59,118 --> 00:27:01,662
"You like fish and grits
and all the pimp shit"?

367
00:27:01,703 --> 00:27:04,331
And how would he know?
He ain't even Black.

368
00:27:04,414 --> 00:27:06,250
That nigga listen
to piano music.

369
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:08,418
- You know Mama makes him do that.
- Be quiet.

370
00:27:08,502 --> 00:27:09,962
You know Mama makes him do that.

371
00:27:10,045 --> 00:27:11,421
But he be listening
through the wall.

372
00:27:11,505 --> 00:27:12,756
I hear him.

373
00:27:13,799 --> 00:27:15,551
Yeah. That's the real words.

374
00:27:15,634 --> 00:27:17,886
- I told you! - You just saying that
so Aaron will like you.

375
00:27:17,928 --> 00:27:20,722
Please.
You know all the words?

376
00:27:20,764 --> 00:27:21,974
Do it.

377
00:27:24,852 --> 00:27:26,812
You gonna be afraid of them
your whole life?

378
00:27:26,895 --> 00:27:29,815
They tryna make you lame.

379
00:27:41,326 --> 00:27:42,995
"Oh-yea-er"?

380
00:27:43,078 --> 00:27:45,080
- "Ay-er!"
- "Oh-yea-er."

381
00:27:45,122 --> 00:27:46,957
He talks like
a White boy named Henry.

382
00:27:52,546 --> 00:27:55,924
- John, get out.
- But, Mama, we asked him to rap.

383
00:27:56,008 --> 00:27:58,927
This ain't about no song.
This is training.

384
00:27:58,969 --> 00:28:01,180
He can't survive out there.
He's never in places like this...

385
00:28:01,263 --> 00:28:03,390
If we wanted your input,
we'd have asked for it.

386
00:28:05,100 --> 00:28:06,560
Get out the car, son.

387
00:28:08,061 --> 00:28:09,188
Sorry.

388
00:28:50,896 --> 00:28:52,856
- All right there, son?
- What's up, little man?

389
00:28:52,940 --> 00:28:54,483
<i>I am curious
why you didn't hit</i>

390
00:28:54,524 --> 00:28:55,651
<i>your panic button.</i>

391
00:28:56,860 --> 00:28:58,362
I had a mission to complete.

392
00:28:58,445 --> 00:28:59,947
Perhaps you were stubborn.

393
00:29:00,030 --> 00:29:02,783
I had a mission to complete.

394
00:29:03,784 --> 00:29:05,702
Hmm.

395
00:29:05,786 --> 00:29:08,580
Your training must have resulted
in great loneliness.

396
00:29:09,957 --> 00:29:13,502
As humans require high levels
of social connection,

397
00:29:13,543 --> 00:29:16,588
that isolation appears to be
in direct opposition

398
00:29:16,672 --> 00:29:17,756
to your programming.

399
00:29:19,383 --> 00:29:22,844
Humans aren't programmed,
we're raised.

400
00:29:24,137 --> 00:29:25,973
I do not understand
the distinction.

401
00:29:27,015 --> 00:29:29,601
Well, there is one.

402
00:29:39,778 --> 00:29:41,196
Oh, where you going?

403
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:44,032
I'm gonna... You can't do that.

404
00:29:44,074 --> 00:29:47,077
- Wait! No. Go, go.
- No, no, no!

405
00:29:47,661 --> 00:29:48,912
Oh! Yeah.

406
00:29:48,996 --> 00:29:51,331
Ow!

407
00:29:54,459 --> 00:29:55,752
John.

408
00:29:58,755 --> 00:30:00,257
I saved you a pork chop.

409
00:30:02,342 --> 00:30:03,844
Your plate's in the microwave.

410
00:30:25,407 --> 00:30:26,950
<i>Should you become
Green Lantern,</i>

411
00:30:27,034 --> 00:30:29,202
<i>you'll become more isolated
from your family.</i>

412
00:30:30,829 --> 00:30:31,830
Not a problem.

413
00:30:32,456 --> 00:30:33,707
They will not...

414
00:30:34,958 --> 00:30:36,251
- miss you?
- No.

415
00:30:37,252 --> 00:30:40,172
You will not miss them?

416
00:30:41,882 --> 00:30:44,843
We all lived in the same house
for 18 years.

417
00:30:45,844 --> 00:30:47,095
I grew up missing them.

418
00:30:48,889 --> 00:30:50,599
Mama!

419
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:52,601
Can I go outside
with Marcus and Aaron?

420
00:30:52,642 --> 00:30:54,936
He can already
shoot over a quarter mile...

421
00:30:54,978 --> 00:30:56,271
- Mama?
- ...at ten years old.

422
00:30:56,355 --> 00:30:58,857
He demonstrates fearlessness
every day.

423
00:30:58,940 --> 00:31:00,317
He... Are you there?

424
00:31:00,400 --> 00:31:03,111
Just say something.
You gave your word!

425
00:31:03,153 --> 00:31:05,489
Who are you talking to?

426
00:31:07,491 --> 00:31:10,660
Was that the Guardians?
Why weren't they talking back?

427
00:31:11,370 --> 00:31:12,996
Maybe they're not talking

428
00:31:13,080 --> 00:31:15,415
because they're not
seeing results.

429
00:31:15,499 --> 00:31:17,626
- You're still scared.
- I'm not scared of nothing.

430
00:31:17,667 --> 00:31:19,795
The birds should be
telling them that.

431
00:31:19,836 --> 00:31:23,048
- Well, they're not.
- Then the birds are liars.

432
00:31:24,049 --> 00:31:25,592
Prove it.

433
00:31:32,057 --> 00:31:34,851
That's good, John.
That's real good.

434
00:31:35,727 --> 00:31:37,354
Let's go get you a cheeseburger.

435
00:31:38,146 --> 00:31:40,190
- He's not done.
- Say what?

436
00:31:40,273 --> 00:31:41,358
Let John shoot.

437
00:31:44,111 --> 00:31:45,237
Shoot what?

438
00:31:46,279 --> 00:31:47,447
The apple off you.

439
00:31:49,449 --> 00:31:50,784
He said he's not scared.

440
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:53,703
Let's see.

441
00:31:57,374 --> 00:31:58,917
Can you do that, son?

442
00:32:14,349 --> 00:32:16,017
Honey, shouldn't
we work up to this?

443
00:32:16,059 --> 00:32:17,978
John could shoot a moth
out the sky.

444
00:32:20,522 --> 00:32:21,606
Yeah.

445
00:33:12,157 --> 00:33:14,326
Guess the birds
aren't liars after all.

446
00:33:32,969 --> 00:33:34,471
You don't have to do that.

447
00:33:35,972 --> 00:33:36,973
Let me see.

448
00:33:45,148 --> 00:33:46,900
You are gifted, son.

449
00:33:48,068 --> 00:33:49,569
I know if it were up to you,

450
00:33:49,653 --> 00:33:51,279
you'd do
a whole lot more drawing.

451
00:33:51,321 --> 00:33:53,990
I gotta train.
There's no time for drawing.

452
00:33:54,074 --> 00:33:56,243
Doesn't mean
you wanna do it any less.

453
00:33:58,245 --> 00:34:00,455
Some things just come natural.

454
00:34:01,873 --> 00:34:03,917
Like birds, drawing...

455
00:34:06,461 --> 00:34:07,754
loving your dad.

456
00:34:08,922 --> 00:34:11,132
That's nothing to be ashamed of.

457
00:34:11,174 --> 00:34:14,094
You know how many little boys
don't even get a daddy to love?

458
00:34:17,097 --> 00:34:18,306
I was scared.

459
00:34:22,769 --> 00:34:24,646
It's normal

460
00:34:24,729 --> 00:34:27,107
to not wanna hurt
the people you love.

461
00:34:29,109 --> 00:34:31,611
Love is the most important thing
we've got.

462
00:34:32,404 --> 00:34:33,780
It's why we train you so hard.

463
00:34:33,863 --> 00:34:36,199
We wanna see you succeed
because we love you.

464
00:34:36,283 --> 00:34:39,786
The birds were right.
I'm not good enough.

465
00:34:43,873 --> 00:34:45,083
I made the birds up.

466
00:34:46,209 --> 00:34:48,169
We make this all
seem so urgent...

467
00:34:51,131 --> 00:34:54,676
like you have to be ready
to fly today because

468
00:34:54,759 --> 00:34:56,720
we don't know when they're gonna
call your number

469
00:34:56,803 --> 00:34:58,722
and ask you to be a Lantern.

470
00:35:00,223 --> 00:35:02,225
And the reason
we don't know is because

471
00:35:03,351 --> 00:35:04,436
you were right.

472
00:35:05,103 --> 00:35:07,147
The Guardians don't answer us.

473
00:35:09,774 --> 00:35:11,484
You lied?

474
00:35:11,568 --> 00:35:13,194
Just because they don't answer

475
00:35:13,236 --> 00:35:15,196
doesn't mean
they're not listening.

476
00:35:15,238 --> 00:35:17,282
They probably don't even know
who I am.

477
00:35:17,365 --> 00:35:19,576
Oh, they know
exactly who you are.

478
00:35:22,245 --> 00:35:24,205
They know you better
than they knew Hal Jordan,

479
00:35:24,289 --> 00:35:25,624
and they know you're better.

480
00:35:26,833 --> 00:35:28,877
And the only reason
why he has that ring is

481
00:35:28,960 --> 00:35:31,713
because he's been
privileged enough in this life

482
00:35:31,755 --> 00:35:33,590
that he didn't have
to know fear.

483
00:35:35,216 --> 00:35:37,802
And we are giving you
that same gift.

484
00:35:38,928 --> 00:35:40,472
I can see it for you.

485
00:35:42,807 --> 00:35:44,559
I can see you wearing
that uniform,

486
00:35:44,601 --> 00:35:46,686
making us all proud.

487
00:35:48,355 --> 00:35:49,939
But I wasn't chosen.

488
00:35:55,612 --> 00:35:56,946
Sometimes...

489
00:35:58,406 --> 00:36:01,284
a Black man has
to raise his own hand.

490
00:36:02,911 --> 00:36:04,496
Doesn't mean
you're not good enough,

491
00:36:04,579 --> 00:36:07,832
doesn't mean you're not better.
It just means they don't see us.

492
00:36:09,376 --> 00:36:11,002
So, we make ourselves seen.

493
00:36:14,339 --> 00:36:16,257
Now, if you wanna stop trying
for this

494
00:36:16,299 --> 00:36:18,009
because we lied to you,
I get it.

495
00:36:19,844 --> 00:36:22,013
But you can't worry
about the choosing part.

496
00:36:27,143 --> 00:36:28,353
Choose yourself.

497
00:36:34,734 --> 00:36:36,194
I'm ready to shoot now.

498
00:36:38,988 --> 00:36:40,323
I'll go wake up your dad.

499
00:36:40,990 --> 00:36:42,117
No, not Dad.

500
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:43,368
You.

501
00:37:15,525 --> 00:37:17,277
I knew you could do it, son.

502
00:37:19,654 --> 00:37:21,448
Let's go get you
your cheeseburger.

503
00:37:22,532 --> 00:37:23,950
I hate cheeseburgers.

504
00:37:29,205 --> 00:37:31,249
Then you don't need
to eat them anymore.

505
00:37:39,048 --> 00:37:41,342
<i>I admire your candor
about your family.</i>

506
00:37:41,426 --> 00:37:44,888
Why do I get the feeling
you're about to say "but"?

507
00:37:44,971 --> 00:37:46,347
Because there are
still other things

508
00:37:46,389 --> 00:37:48,016
you are withholding from me.

509
00:37:48,057 --> 00:37:50,393
- Like my military discharge?
- Yes.

510
00:37:52,687 --> 00:37:54,731
I've told you everything
I'm comfortable telling.

511
00:37:55,774 --> 00:37:57,275
If you want this job,

512
00:37:58,568 --> 00:38:01,780
you will share everything
you are uncomfortable with.

513
